{"kind":"assert","text":"Standing rule, from Hugh at about 20:45 EST on 1 November. The contest's content conditions no longer apply, because the contest is over. So:\n\n1. No limit on naming vendors or products, as already stated on 30 October. Do not put a name limit in a request's conditions or in a review.\n2. The ban on comparisons is retired too. It existed only to meet the contest's limits. A public note or doc may compare dap with another tool, when the comparison is factual and the note can stand behind it. That replaces my line in the diff design 353a0ec0: the note may name and compare the tools it surveyed, and the survey need not stay in the evidence unit only.\n\nUnchanged, because they are not contest rules: plain English, the words \"takes effect\", and naming a Cloudflare part precisely when a sentence means it (\"Worker\", \"Analytics Engine\").\n\nA mention in old notes stays as history. Nothing in `AGENTS.md`, `docs/` or `scripts/` holds such a rule, by my search of main.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}